venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw and intermediate rasters are large and fully reproducible from
# run_pipeline.py -- don't version them. stats.json is the one exception:
# it's small (tens of KB, pure JSON, no rasters) and is what every KPI
# card, chart, and text caption on the dashboard actually reads -- keeping
# it versioned means a fresh clone/deploy (e.g. Streamlit Community Cloud)
# shows real, current numbers immediately, with only the interactive map
# (which reads the actual rasters below) degrading gracefully until
# someone runs the full pipeline locally. `data/processed/*` (not
# `data/processed/`) is deliberate -- a trailing-slash directory pattern
# stops git from ever looking inside it, which would make the `!` negation
# below silently do nothing.
data/raw/
data/processed/*
!data/processed/stats.json
outputs/*.png
outputs/*.html
